"""Auto-generated FF9 model-alias registry: the engine's model-name -> donor-prefab rename chain.

DO NOT EDIT BY HAND. Regenerate with:  python -m ff9mapkit._regen_modelalias --memoria <path>
Source: Memoria Assembly-CSharp/Global/Model/ModelFactory.cs (upscaleTable / revertUpscaleTable /
GetNameFromFF9DBALL / GetGEOID / GetRenameModelPath, open-source) -- Memoria's reverse-engineered
name->name interop labels; NOT extracted game data (see docs/PROVENANCE.md).

~103 GEO catalog ids ship no prefab under their own id: a character BATTLE form's body is the
same prefab its FIELD form loads (GEO_MAIN_B0_000 -> GEO_MAIN_UP0_ZDN -> GEO_MAIN_F0_ZDN = 98),
bosses borrow character bodies, Zidane's alt outfits share 98, three accessories point at their
F1 twin. The engine resolves a requested name UP into the HD-rename space (UPSCALE =
CheckUpscale) then back DOWN to the shipping prefab (REVERT_UPSCALE, falling back to
DBALL_SWITCH + a second revert = GetRenameModelPath/GetNameFromFF9DBALL); GEOID_SPECIALS pins
two names the GEO table never lists; SUB_TYPE_GEO_IDS forces the two mask prefabs into
models/5/. Sole reader: ff9mapkit.models.extract.resolve_prefab -- animations and identity keep
the REQUESTED id (resolve_geo); only the GEOMETRY location goes through this chain.
"""

